# RRF macro / meta-command rules

## Macro parameters are read-only

`param.X` comes from `M98 … X…` (or DWC). **Never assign to it.**

```gcode
; BAD — Error: Bad command: param.S = 235
if !exists(param.S)
    param.S = 235

; GOOD
var temp = 235
if exists(param.S)
	set var.temp = param.S
```

Reserved / awkward M98 letters: **P** (filename) and **R** (restartable). Prefer other letters (S, B, D, N, …).

## Locals use var / set

```gcode
var band = 235
set var.band = param.B   ; only after exists(param.B)
echo {var.band}
M303 H1 S{var.temp}
```

## Daemon GPIO during long moves

In `sys/daemon.g`, use expression form so the loop is not synced to the motion queue:

```gcode
M42 P{2} S{1}
G4 P{200}
```

Not `M42 P2 S1` / `G4 S0.2`.

## Dual-zone heater PID (FGF pellet)

Tool 0 = H1 band + H2 nozzle. Large thermal mass — **not** FDM-hotend timing.

Tune from cold via `macros/Heater tuning/` **1 → 2 → 3**. Macros set a high `M307 … D` (default H1 D120) before `M303` so RRF does not cancel with “target temperature was not reached”. Override: `M98 P"…" D180`.

Copy each Console `M307` into `config.g`. See README “Dual-zone extruder PID”.
